-- title:
--   Kummer independence of p from inertia-fixed units
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $N$ be a natural number, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `P.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the nonunits of $P$, so that $P$ sits above the rational prime $p$. Write $I_P$ for `P.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained as the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\zeta$ be a primitive $p^N$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $t$ be a natural number, and let $u, \beta : \mathrm{Fin}\, t \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be families such that each $u_i$ has $P$-valuation equal to $1$, each $u_i$ is fixed by every element of $I_P$, and $\beta_i^{\,p^N} = u_i$. Let $\varpi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfy $\varpi^{p^N} = p$. Then there exists $\tau \in I_P$ which fixes every $\xi$ with $\xi^{p^N} = 1$, fixes every $\beta_i$, and satisfies $\tau(\varpi) = \zeta\varpi$.
--
--   This is the construction of the inertia element $\tau$ used in Wiles's local analysis at $p$: over the fixed field of $I_P$ the radicand $p$ is Kummer-independent of the inertia-fixed units $u_i$ at exponent $p^N$, so the Kummer extension generated by $\varpi$ remains of full degree after adjoining $\mu_{p^N}$ and the $p^N$-th roots $\beta_i$. It is used by [`ValuationSubring.sub_one_mul_sum_smul_eq_zero_of_corner_decomposition`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.sub_one_mul_sum_smul_eq_zero_of_corner_decomposition).
